+/**
+ * LOCAL SPIKE PATCH (flutter-maplibre-gl): rebinds the runtime and every
+ * handle it owns (maps, projections, render sessions) to the calling thread.
+ *
+ * Rationale: garbage-collected embedders (Dart isolates) cannot promise a
+ * stable OS thread; the VM may resume an isolate on another pool thread.
+ * Calling this at the start of a turn re-homes the owner-thread affinity.
+ *
+ * Contract:
+ * - No call on the runtime or any of its handles may be in flight.
+ * - The calling thread must not own another live runtime.
+ * - Map projections and render sessions carry no owner link and are re-homed
+ *   globally: the process is assumed to hold a single live runtime.
+ *
+ * Returns:
+ * - MLN_STATUS_OK on success (or when already bound to the calling thread).
+ * - MLN_STATUS_INVALID_ARGUMENT when runtime is null or not a live handle.
+ * - MLN_STATUS_INVALID_STATE when the calling thread owns another runtime.
+ * - MLN_STATUS_NATIVE_ERROR when an internal exception is converted to status.
+ */
+MLN_API mln_status mln_runtime_rebind_thread(mln_runtime* runtime)
+  MLN_NOEXCEPT;
